WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.033
-Our next guest is featured
in season 3 of

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:06.167
"The Standups" available on
Netflix this December.

00:00:06.167 --> 00:00:09.200
Please welcome the very funny
Dusty Slay!

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:17.334
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:19.167
-Alright. Okay.

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:22.167
We're having a good time.
And okay.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.868
Well, I'm pumped to be here.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:26.133
People always tell me I look
like somebody, you know?

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.334
They're always like,
"You look like Joe Dirt."

00:00:28.334 --> 00:00:30.901
Or "You look like
'Wayne's World.'"

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:31.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:34.300
"You look like
Jay and Silent Bob."

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.167
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:39.100
One guy was like, "You look like
a Walmart Billy Ray Cyrus."

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:43.367
I was like, "Dang, I didn't know
you could get more Walmart

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:45.200
than Billy Ray Cyrus."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.567
I thought that was
as Walmart as it got.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:50.100
But people always tell me
I look just like their cousin.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.734
They're always like,
"You look just like my cousin.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:54.634
Just like my cousin."

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:56.434
And then every time
they show me a picture,

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.067
it's never a good-looking dude.

00:00:58.067 --> 00:00:59.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:02.601
I'm always -- I'm never like,
"Man, I appreciate that."

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:05.400
I'm always like, "That's what
you think I look like?

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.334
That's how I look to you?"

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:09.767
You ever see
a bad picture of yourself

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:12.167
and you know that
you don't look like that?

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.767 --> 00:01:16.200
But also deep down inside

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.300
you know that you did
look like that?

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:25.033
[ Applause ]

00:01:25.033 --> 00:01:27.934
I mean, like, that camera
didn't make that up, right?

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:30.601
Like, it might have caught you
in a bad moment,

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:32.834
but that's you in that picture.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:34.601
Now, the question you got to ask
yourself is

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:37.334
"How often am I looking
like that?

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:40.834
And what do I got to do to never
look like that again?"

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:43.167
But people always think
I know about cars.

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:46.100
They think I look like a guy
that knows a lot about cars.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.534
And they'll always ask me to
listen to their car

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:50.834
to see what's wrong with it,
you know?

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:53.567
And I'll do it.
You know what I mean?

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:55.901
Like, I don't want to let them
down, right?

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:57.501
So I'll listen. I go, "Ooh.

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:59.067
You should get that checked out,
man."

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:01.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.133
And if you do it just right,
they'll be like, "You know what?

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:05.501
I will get it checked out.
I appreciate that.

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.901
I wasn't. But I will now."

00:02:07.901 --> 00:02:09.834
And I know a little bit
about cars

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.300
'cause I wrecked
a bunch of them.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.701
I feel like if you wreck enough,

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:16.734
you learn what a car can do,
what it can't do.

00:02:16.734 --> 00:02:19.200
What it can't come back from,
you know?

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.901
And for a while I was driving
a 1982 Buick LeSabre.

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:24.133
[ Man cheers]
Alright.

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.501
Real big car, you know?
Used a lot of gas.

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:28.067
And I used to make this joke
at work.

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:29.801
I'd be like,
"Man, that car uses so much gas,

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.834
I bet it's using gas right now
in the parking lot."

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:33.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.000
That's a great work joke.
People love that.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.801
One guy didn't get it, though.

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:39.400
He goes,
"Hell, you might have a leak."

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:44.934
I was like,
"No, I don't think so."

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:48.667
But I did have a car that leaked
a lot of oil for a while.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.067
And I like that in a car.

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:53.868
Like, you leak a little oil,
pour a little in there.

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:56.167
Leak a little oil,
pour a little in there.

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:57.701
Never get an oil change.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:03:05.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:07.267
People are like, "When is
the last time you changed

00:03:07.267 --> 00:03:08.267
the oil on this car?"

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.834
I'm like,
"It's changing right now."

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:14.601
Okay? This car is efficient.

00:03:14.601 --> 00:03:16.601
I used to drive that car
all over the country.

00:03:16.601 --> 00:03:18.133
You know, leaking oil
everywhere.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:20.601
I drove up to Duluth, Minnesota,
one time.

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:21.701
-Yeah!
-Alright.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.801
And I went to this aquarium.

00:03:23.801 --> 00:03:25.400
I don't know if you've been
there before.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.701
I don't know if I'd go
just for the aquarium,

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:30.100
but if you're up there,
check it out.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.767
It was a nice place, but it just
felt like the aquarium

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:35.234
was on a two-week notice, right?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:38.334
They're like, "We about to shut
this place down."

00:03:38.334 --> 00:03:40.067
Like, some animals were missing.

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.167
There was a fountain
that had dried up.

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:44.000
There was a turtle in there.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.534
I didn't know if it was ceramic

00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:47.400
or if it had just stopped
moving.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:52.133
And they had a walk-in bird cage
that you could walk into.

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:53.567
But I got in there,
and it just felt like

00:03:53.567 --> 00:03:56.901
it was birds from the outside.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.901 --> 00:04:01.033
Like, I know all birds are
from the outside.

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:03.901
But it felt like you were in,
like, a retail store

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:07.067
and a bird had just flown in

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:09.767
and then couldn't figure
how to get out.

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.801
And then I went to
the main aquarium

00:04:11.801 --> 00:04:13.434
and I'm looking at
the fish tank, right?

00:04:13.434 --> 00:04:14.934
And there's a lot of fish
in there.

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:17.601
And this girl comes up to me
and she has a name tag on.

00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:21.868
And the name tag has her name,
and then it says "fish expert."

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:24.067
I was like, "Alright, that's
what I'm talking about."

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:26.133
You know what I mean?
I don't run into a lot of

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:27.834
fish experts out
here in the world.

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.734
And I thought, "This is a great
time to get some answers

00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:31.334
to some of the fish questions
that I have."

00:04:31.334 --> 00:04:36.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:38.000
So I started asking her
some stuff,

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.634
you know, stuff I can Google.

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:43.367
But I thought, "Hey, let's have
a real human experience here."

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:46.400
So I start asking her stuff, and
then I say, "Oh, you know what?

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.968
I got a good one."
This is a good question.

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:49.868
You're going to like this.
This is what I said to her.

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:51.467
I go, "Let me ask you this.

00:04:51.467 --> 00:04:53.334
Do fish sleep?"

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:56.300
That's what I said to her.
I said, "Do fish sleep?"

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.901
And she looked me straight
in the face and she goes,

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:02.000
"I don't know 'cause I don't
work here at night."

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:06.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:08.834
Okay, hey, thank you very much,
guys.

00:05:08.834 --> 00:05:11.834
I appreciate you. Thank you.
Thank you, guys.

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:14.400
Thank you.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.601
-Dusty Slay, everybody.

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:18.501
Dusty Slay.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:18.501 --> 00:05:21.968
Season 3 of "The Standups" is
out December on Netflix.

